WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.850
There's a different method of talking

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:04.830
about coins; you know you could- you can

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:06.899
imagine somebody spinning a coin on its

00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:08.910
edge and seeing does it come up heads or

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.010
tails? And if you're me you could ask,

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.900
well, you know, what are the odds if a

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.969
coin is spun on its edge what are the

00:00:14.969 --> 00:00:17.369
odds it comes up heads or tails? Now

00:00:17.369 --> 00:00:19.369
there's a right answer to that question.

00:00:19.369 --> 00:00:22.760
You don't know, because you don't know.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.470
Magicians have coins which are slightly

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:29.880
shaved; and you can't feel it, you can't

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.590
see it but the coin always comes up

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.110
tails when it's spun on its edge. It has

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.910
to do, in a very delicate way, where the

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.469
center of gravity of the coin is.

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:39.899
Determining that is a completely

00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:43.710
different physics task, math task. We have

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.450
done it experimentally, it's not so easy

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:50.030
to do the math of it, and experimentally

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:53.219
coins are quite biased. And that's an

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.170
easy experiment to do; you can get a

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:56.670
class of kids, and I've done it with a

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:58.530
class of a hundred students. A given coin

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.449
has its own bias when spun on the edge,

00:01:00.449 --> 00:01:03.390
but that bias fluctuates from coin to

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:05.790
coin and there- it's easy to find coins

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:09.689
which are 80% tails. Just they're slightly

00:01:09.689 --> 00:01:12.540
you know bevelled. Pennies 
and nickels- coins,

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:15.600
American coins, which 
have unbevelled edges,

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.630
this coin has a serrated edge. Coins

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.880
which have unserrated edges tend to be

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.710
more biased and it- so
that, you know, if

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:23.850
you just happen to have one in your

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.799
pocket well, you know, who pays for the

00:01:25.799 --> 00:01:27.509
drinks right? Or whatever. I'm going to

00:01:27.509 --> 00:01:31.020
combine those two ideas; if I asked you

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:34.409
before this interview which do you think

00:01:34.409 --> 00:01:36.930
is fairer? A coin caught in the hand or a

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:40.079
coin allowed to drop on to the table? We

00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:42.540
can do that a few times so you can, you

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.850
know, catch it, try to
catch it. You know, a coin

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:45.930
allowed to do that.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:48.000
Well first of all most people, if asked

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.000
which is fairer just think this guy's

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.040
nuts, that question doesn't make sense.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.810
You know, they're both kind of pretty

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:58.200
fair. But if pressed people when pushed

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.270
seem to think that a coin dropping on

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.579
the floor is fairer. And I'd like to

00:02:02.579 --> 00:02:05.100
suggest that when- why do people guess

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.960
that, that when somebody catches a coin

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.349
in their hand there's a hand there. And

00:02:09.349 --> 00:02:11.940
it might be that you can adjust your

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.980
hand or do something,

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.689
let's rule that out. okay? You're just

00:02:16.689 --> 00:02:18.370
flipping coins for yourself, you're not

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:20.409
trying to cheat anybody. If you flip a

00:02:20.409 --> 00:02:22.269
coin this way or if you flip a coin and

00:02:22.269 --> 00:02:24.730
let it land on the floor, does it make

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:26.500
any sense to talk about is one fairer

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:30.159
than the other? But when a coin hits the

00:02:30.159 --> 00:02:31.659
ground, because I watch them - and if you

00:02:31.659 --> 00:02:33.069
had your camera we could watch them

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:44.980
together - before it dies, often it spins

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:47.319
around on its edge before dying; and some

00:02:47.319 --> 00:02:50.169
of that edge bias comes in. And so

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:51.970
there's a real sense in which coins

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:54.099
landing on the floor are less fair than

00:02:54.099 --> 00:02:55.959
coins caught in the air. Well there's

00:02:55.959 --> 00:02:57.789
something to think about.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.980
[Preview]..fast it was traveling,
you know, say in feet per

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.469
second. And if you knew how many times a

00:03:04.469 --> 00:03:07.230
second it was turning over, Newton tells

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:09.870
you, if you know the speed, how long it

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.819
takes to come down and if you know how

00:03:11.819 --> 00:03:13.530
fast it's turning you know whether it'll

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:16.489
come up heads or tails.

